WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:07.272
In the Eastern Jin, the poet Tao Yuanming served as magistrate of Pengze, and his monthly salary was only five pecks of rice.

00:00:07.622 --> 00:00:13.406
One day, his superiors sent an inspector to examine the county, and the man put on very grand airs.

00:00:13.756 --> 00:00:17.836
The moment the inspector stepped down from his sedan chair, he began finding fault with this and that.

00:00:18.186 --> 00:00:24.930
Someone urged Tao Yuanming to put on neat official robes and go out to welcome the inspector with utmost respect.

00:00:25.280 --> 00:00:29.408
Hearing this, Tao Yuanming quietly put down the brush in his hand.

00:00:29.758 --> 00:00:37.246
Tao Yuanming shook his head and said: I cannot, for the sake of this salary of five pecks of rice, bow my head and bend my back to such a petty man.

00:00:37.596 --> 00:00:42.420
His voice was not loud, yet it was so firm that everyone present fell silent.

00:00:42.770 --> 00:00:48.290
With that, he took off his official hat, hung it on the wall, resigned that very day, and went home.

00:00:48.640 --> 00:00:53.800
The moment he walked out of the office, he felt incomparably light at heart.

00:00:54.150 --> 00:01:02.718
From then on he lived in rural seclusion, growing chrysanthemums and drinking wine; later generations praise his integrity with the words 'never bow for five pecks of rice.'

